@orgA = e312ace9-cf22-4c43-a8fa-6ccdfe6240b8
@orgB = f97b4db1-f3b4-471f-9ca8-bcf59673eff8

### Log in as A
# @name loginA
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "owner@example.com", "password": "CorrectHorse2026" }

### Log in as B
# @name loginB
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "second@example.com", "password": "CorrectHorse2026" }

### 1. A creates a property (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/properties
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "A Court" }

### 2. B creates a property in B's own organization (expect 201)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/properties
Authorization: Bearer {{loginB.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgB}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "B Towers" }

### 3. A lists properties, code has NO filter (expect ONLY "A Court")
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/properties
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 4. B lists properties in B's organization (expect ONLY "B Towers")
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/properties
Authorization: Bearer {{loginB.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgB}}

### 5. Forgot withOrg (expect an empty list: fails closed)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/properties-no-context
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA.response.body.$.accessToken}}

### 6. B reaches into A's organization as a TENANT and lists (expect "A Court", read allowed here)
GET http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/properties
Authorization: Bearer {{loginB.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgA}}

### 7. B as TENANT tries to create in A (expect 403, role check)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/properties
Authorization: Bearer {{loginB.response.body.$.accessToken}}
X-Organization-Id: {{orgA}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Hacked Property" }

### 8. Smuggling an organization into the body (expect 422, strict schema)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/demo/properties
Authorization: Bearer {{loginA.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sneaky", "organizationId": "{{orgB}}" }

### 9. Login still works under RLS (expect 200)
POST http://localhost:4000/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "owner@example.com", "password": "CorrectHorse2026" }